# Document everything

When you change behaviour in `src/astro/`, update documentation in the same task before finishing. Do not treat docs as optional follow-up work.

## When to update docs

Update documentation for any change that affects:

- CLI commands, flags, or output
- Pipeline contract, step/filter APIs, or file I/O
- Storage layout, run lifecycle, or statistics
- Security or trust boundaries
- Public Python exports (`astro.__all__`)
- Installation, packaging, or release process

## Where to update

| Change type | Update |
|-------------|--------|
| User-facing behaviour | Relevant page in `docs/user-guide/` or `docs/getting-started/` |
| Behavioural contract | `SPEC.md` (clarifications only unless approved) |
| CLI surface | `docs/user-guide/cli.md` (canonical); `README.md` only for a brief command list |
| Public API | Docstrings in `src/astro/` and `docs/api/index.md` if exports change |
| Examples | `examples/` and `examples/README.md` |
| User-visible release | `CHANGELOG.md` |
| Contributor workflow | `docs/contributing/` (canonical); `CONTRIBUTING.md` and `AGENTS.md` stay short |

## Workflow

1. Read the relevant `SPEC.md` section and matching user guide page before coding.
2. Implement the code change (with tests first per test-first rule).
3. Update every doc location from the table above that the change touches.
4. Grep `docs/`, `README.md`, `SPEC.md`, and `CHANGELOG.md` for stale references (old flags, removed APIs, "not implemented", wrong version).
5. If CLI options changed, verify `docs/user-guide/cli.md` matches `src/astro/cli/main.py`.
6. Run `make docs` when Sphinx pages or cross-references changed.

## Checklist before completing

- [ ] User guide reflects the new or changed behaviour
- [ ] `SPEC.md` matches implementation (or only clarifies existing intent)
- [ ] `CHANGELOG.md` updated for user-visible changes
- [ ] `README.md` updated only when install links or high-level overview need changing (not long-form guides)
- [ ] Root markdown files (`README.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`) link to `docs/` rather than duplicating guide content
- [ ] Public API docstrings present for new or changed exports
- [ ] No stale "stub", "not implemented", or outdated version references remain

## Example

Adding `astro cleanup --dry-run`:

1. Add test in `tests/cli/test_commands.py`
2. Implement in `src/astro/cli/main.py`
3. Update `docs/user-guide/cli.md`, `SPEC.md` CLI table, and `CHANGELOG.md`
4. Add the flag to the brief command list in `README.md` only if it is a primary workflow command
